  partName: Left Rear Bolt 2
  description: The Left Rear Bolt 2 is another tiny, complex-shaped component positioned
    at the top-left-rear of the engine, fabricated from Material.001, which serves
    as a supplementary fastener for the engine's rear section, providing additional
    support and reinforcement to the existing bolts, and its complex shape facilitates
    a secure connection with adjacent components. The presence of this bolt underscores
    the importance of redundancy in critical engine components. Interestingly, the
    Left Rear Bolt 2 is often overlooked during routine maintenance, despite its
    vital role in ensuring the engine's overall stability.
